Day 01 - Setting Up Python Virtual Environment (venv) Objective

Today, I learned how to create a Python Virtual Environment (venv) to manage project dependencies separately from the system Python installation.

What is a Virtual Environment?
A virtual environment is an isolated Python environment that allows a project to have its own packages and dependencies without affecting other Python projects on the same machine.

Why do we need a Virtual Environment?

* Avoid package version conflicts between projects.
* Keep project dependencies isolated.
* Make projects easier to share and reproduce.
* Maintain a clean system-wide Python installation.
* Follow industry best practices for Python development.

Command Used
Create a Virtual Environment
--------------------
python -m venv venv
--------------------

Activate the Virtual Environment (Windows)
---------------------------
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
--------------------------

Deactivate the Virtual Environment
------------
deactivate
-----------

